<section class="rcx-mush" aria-label="The mushrooms"><div class="rcx-m m-lions-mane"><div class="rcx-symt"><img class="rcx-sym" src="{{ 'rcx-sym-lions-mane.svg' | asset_url }}" alt=""></div><h3>LION'S MANE</h3><p class="lat">Hericium erinaceus</p><p class="pp"><b>PART</b> FRUITING BODY<br><b>PROCESS</b> HOT WATER + ALCOHOL<br><b>PACKET</b> 2 GRAMS</p><p class="ab">Lion's mane carries two kinds of compounds. Hot water draws out the beta&#8209;glucans. Alcohol draws out the ones water can't reach. Published research on lion's mane looks at both, so ours is extracted both&nbsp;ways.</p><div class="lab"><span>Hericium erinaceus fruiting body</span><span>80:20 water alcohol extract</span><span>Beta&#8209;glucan / Megazyme K&#8209;YBGL</span><span>Heavy metals / ICP&#8209;MS ISO 17294&#8209;2</span><span>539 pesticides / EN 15662, EN 12393</span></div><a class="rcx-shop" href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}#lions-mane">SHOP LION'S MANE</a></div><div class="rcx-m m-cordyceps"><div class="rcx-symt"><img class="rcx-sym" src="{{ 'rcx-sym-cordyceps.svg' | asset_url }}" alt=""></div><h3>CORDYCEPS</h3><p class="lat">Cordyceps militaris</p><p class="pp"><b>PART</b> FRUITING BODY<br><b>PROCESS</b> HOT WATER<br><b>PACKET</b> 2 GRAMS</p><p class="ab">Cordyceps militaris is grown for its fruiting body, where its best&#8209;known compound, cordycepin, is found. Cordycepin dissolves in hot water, the same method used in the published research. So that's how we extract&nbsp;it.</p><div class="lab"><span>Cordyceps militaris fruiting body</span><span>Hot water extract</span><span>Beta&#8209;glucan / Megazyme K&#8209;YBGL</span><span>Cordycepin, adenosine / HPLC</span><span>Heavy metals / ICP&#8209;MS ISO 17294&#8209;2</span><span>539 pesticides / EN 15662, EN 12393</span></div><a class="rcx-shop" href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}#cordyceps">SHOP CORDYCEPS</a></div><div class="rcx-m m-turkey-tail"><div class="rcx-symt"><img class="rcx-sym" src="{{ 'rcx-sym-turkey-tail.svg' | asset_url }}" alt=""></div><h3>TURKEY TAIL</h3><p class="lat">Trametes versicolor</p><p class="pp"><b>PART</b> MYCELIUM<br><b>PROCESS</b> HOT WATER<br><b>PACKET</b> 2 GRAMS</p><p class="ab">The best&#8209;known turkey tail research was done on hot water extracts made from the mycelium, the part that grows below the surface. That's the part we use, and hot water is how we extract&nbsp;it.</p><div class="lab"><span>Trametes versicolor mycelium</span><span>Hot water extract</span><span>Beta&#8209;glucan / Megazyme K&#8209;YBGL</span><span>Heavy metals / ICP&#8209;MS ISO 17294&#8209;2</span><span>539 pesticides / EN 15662, EN 12393</span></div><a class="rcx-shop" href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}#turkey-tail">SHOP TURKEY TAIL</a></div></section>

<section class="rcx-box rcx-whybox">
<p class="rcx-side rcx-side-r" aria-hidden="true"><span class="ln">*Some areas are blurred for legal reasons.</span> <span class="ln">We are still completing the steps that bring</span> <span class="ln">our brand into full focus. Launching February&nbsp;2027.</span></p>
<h2 class="dsh" data-sweep><span>WHY ONE INGREDIENT?</span></h2>
<p>Look at the back of most mushroom products. Ten mushrooms in one scoop. Lion's mane, cordyceps, reishi, chaga and six more. It sounds like you're getting the best of all of them. Now do the math. Split one scoop ten ways and each mushroom gets a sliver, not to mention the grain and other filler routinely added. It reads like abundance. It works like a smoke screen. When everything is in there, nobody can tell you how much of any one thing you're getting, and nobody has&nbsp;to.</p>
<p>Ours has one ingredient. The mushroom. <span class="rcx-ob" aria-hidden="true">Qz'v</span> <span class="rcx-ob" aria-hidden="true">qzvkxwjhb</span> <span class="rcx-ob" aria-hidden="true">qzvkxwj,</span> a full 2 grams of one mushroom, measured into one clean packet to take anywhere you&nbsp;go.</p>
<p>Nothing to carry it, nothing to fill it out, no binders, no flow agents, no anti&#8209;caking agents. And to prove it, we will publish the independent lab report we call the receipts, just one scan away. Build your own honest blend and bring the best of the forest to your coffee, tea or&nbsp;smoothie.</p>
<p class="rcx-prove" data-sweep><span><span class="pl">THEY PROMISE.</span> <span class="pl">WE PROVE.</span></span></p>
</section>
<section class="rcx-box">
<p class="rcx-kick">THE LINE</p>
<h2 class="dsh" data-sweep><span>THE HOLY TRINITY OF MUSHROOMS</span></h2>
<p>We launched with these three mushrooms because we believe them to be the holy trinity of mycological research. Sure, we could have ground up a multitude of mushrooms and who knows what else and called it a super blend like everyone else. The market is flooded with them. But crowd ten mushrooms into one scoop and each one gets only a fraction of a serving, often too little to matter. We chose to go against that trend. We extract species by species for max absorption, the way published research suggests. We provide your mind and body with something worthy of your attention. A packet bold enough to pack a punch. A full single serving of nature's raw harvest. Turkey tail for the crowded airport and the long flight. Lion's mane for when you need to me<span class="rcx-ob" aria-hidden="true">qzvkxw</span> lo<span class="rcx-ob" aria-hidden="true">qz</span> in. Cordyceps for the early start and the long day. Chosen for an ever&#8209;changing world that won't slow&nbsp;down.</p>
